msgid "Secrets in configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use encrypted configuration values to protect sensitive passwords, secrets, "
"tokens and keys."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A secret configuration may be expressed as `${handler::value}`, where the "
"`handler` is the name of a\n"
"`io.smallrye.config.SecretKeysHandler` to decode or decrypt the `value`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Encrypt Configuration values"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To encrypt and later decrypt configuration values, add the following managed "
"dependency:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Use the Quarkus CLI command to add a new encrypted value or encrypt an "
"existent value in `application.properties`:"
msgstr ""

msgid "CLI"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"_For more information about how to install the Quarkus CLI and use it, "
"please refer to xref:cli-tooling.adoc[the Quarkus CLI guide]._"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The configuration property `my.secret` will be added to `application."
"properties` with the value `1234` encrypted and\n"
"encoded in *Base64* and an expression `${aes-gcm-nopadding::}`, with the "
"required secret handler to decrypt the value.\n"
"If it doesn't exist, an encryption key is also generated and set into\n"
"`smallrye.config.secret-handler.aes-gcm-nopadding.encryption-key`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Read Encrypted Configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus configuration system, will automatically decrypt the configuration "
"value when looking up `my.secret`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The encryption key used to encrypt the value must be the same used to "
"decrypt the value and set into\n"
"`smallrye.config.secret-handler.aes-gcm-nopadding.encryption-key`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Returns the value `1234`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Store secrets in a Keystore"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"While having encrypted values, is better than plain values, we would still "
"like to avoid having these set up in\n"
"`application.properties`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Java KeyStore is used as a file-based `Vault`. Sensitive data can be "
"imported to and securely stored in this `Vault`\n"
"as Java `SecretKey` values. To use the `KeyStore` `ConfigSource` add the "
"following managed dependency:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Create a KeyStore"
msgstr ""

msgid "The following command creates a simple KeyStore:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `-alias my.secret` option stores the configuration property name `my."
"secret` in the KeyStore with the value\n"
"`DLTb_9zxThxeT5iAQqswEl5Dn1ju4FdM9hIyVip35t5V`. The `-storepass "
"arealpassword` is the password required to access the keystore."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We also need to safely store the encryption key. You shouldn't store the key "
"with the rest of the secrets, so we can\n"
"create another `KeyStore` for the key:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use the KeyStore"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To use the newly created `KeyStore`s, add the following configuration to "
"`application.properties`:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The path to the ´KeyStore` with properties secrets"
msgstr ""

msgid "The `KeyStore` password to be able to extract the `KeyStore` secrets"
msgstr ""

msgid "The `SecretKeyHandler` to decrypt the `KeyStore` secrets"
msgstr ""

msgid "The path to the ´KeyStore` with encryption key."
msgstr ""

msgid "The `KeyStore` password to be able to extract the encryption key"
msgstr ""

msgid "Protect the KeyStore password"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You need to specify a `KeyStore` password in `application.properties` for "
"Quarkus be able to extract secrets from the\n"
"keystore. This keystore password is a sensitive value, and therefore you "
"should consider how to minimize a risk of\n"
"leaking it and how to protect it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"One important thing you should be aware of is that leaking this password "
"does not necessarily mean the actual secrets\n"
"stored in the keystore will also be leaked since an unauthorized person will "
"also need to access the actual keystore\n"
"file. Restricting access to the keystore file to a limited number of roles "
"and having Quarkus processes running in one\n"
"of these roles will make it harder for anyone outside the group access the "
"keystore. The keystore password can be set\n"
"as an environment variable and this password should be periodically changed "
"to limit a window during which an attacker\n"
"can try to get to the keystore."
msgstr ""
